Yes! Here is the recipe for Olive Garden Alfredo sauce that you can make at home: 
1 block of frozen tallegio cheese, thawed and cut into small pieces
2 tablespoons of butter
2 cloves of garlic, minced
½ cup of heavy cream
2 cups of Parmesan cheese
¼ teaspoon of sea salt

//Step 1:// Melt the butter over medium heat and add the garlic. Cook for about 1 minute until the garlic is fragrant.

//Step2:// Gradually add the heavy cream and cook until the sauce is thickened. 

//Step 3:// Add in the Parmesan cheese and sea salt. Stir to combine.

//Step 4:// Add the thawed tallegio cheese cubes to the sauce and cook until melted.

//Step 5:// Transfer the sauce to a bowl and serve!
